  "views.lifeOfATree.centre": "the year",
  "views.lifeOfATree.foot": "Winter is not a gap between growing seasons — it is part of the cycle. A fruit tree that does not get cold enough for long enough blooms raggedly or not at all, which is why the loop starts there.",
  "views.lifeOfATree.surviveQ": "Will it survive here?",
  "views.lifeOfATree.surviveA": "Every winter on record has a coldest night, and a cultivar has a limit. The answer is how often the first went below the second — nine winters in ten is a different proposition from five.",
  "views.lifeOfATree.fruitQ": "Will it fruit here?",
  "views.lifeOfATree.fruitA": "Hours at or below 45 °F over the winter — the <b>chill</b> on the nursery tag. Too few and the tree wakes unevenly. Vermont has chill to spare; Georgia is where it decides.",
