  "views.lifeOfAnAnimal.claim": "A bird does not read a thermometer.",
  "views.lifeOfAnAnimal.intro": "Almost everything else on this site runs on heat. Animals are the exception. A migrating bird leaves on day length. Day length is the same on the same date every year, whatever the weather did. The insects it arrives to eat came out on warmth, and warmth moves by weeks. In some years the two line up. In others they do not, and that gap is something a grower can watch for.",
