  "views.lifeOfADisease.intro": "A spore on a dry leaf waits. It needs a film of water, or air near saturation, for long enough to germinate and get in — and the warmer it is, the fewer hours that takes. So disease weather is measured in hours of wetness at a temperature, not in degree days.",
  "views.lifeOfADisease.axis": "Hours the leaf stays wet →",
